## Model card

- **Name:** GLM-5.3-FlashX-Legal / GLM-Legal.
- **Short description:** Z.ai's legal-domain model for document understanding, legal reasoning, contract review, and drafting. The publisher explicitly describes legal mid-training and post-training/RL, making this a distinct specialization rather than merely a price or speed tier. Legal specialization is not one of the production tree's deferred voice/finance/health/cyber suffixes.[1]
- **Provider / access:** Native Z.ai Chat Completions and OpenRouter's exact legal route; the publisher also offers an AutoClaw legal workspace and legal MCP integrations. Application tools are separate from the model. No authenticated inference performed.[1][2]
- **Release / knowledge:** Gateway canonical listing date **2026-11-02**; exact original native release day and training knowledge cutoff not independently verified.[2]
- **IDs:** Native `glm-5.3-flashx-legal`; OpenRouter `z-ai/glm-5.3-flashx-legal`. No exact Zen Free ID verified.[1][2]
- **Context window:** Exact gateway record **1,048,576 total / 131,072 maximum output**, corroborating the shared publisher card's 1M/128K limits. No exact legal-model full-window retrieval score found.[1][2]
- **Modalities:** Text, image, video in; text out. The shared native guide additionally describes files. Exact gateway controls include reasoning, tools, and structured output, with max/high/low efforts listed. No native audio or media generation verified.[1][2]
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-11):** Official legal-model pricing row and gateway agree on **$0.37 input / $1.25 output / $0.075 cached input per 1M tokens**. Free cached-input storage on the native table is not free inference. No model-specific ZDR/no-training guarantee assessed.[2][3]
- **Architecture:** Legal-domain mid/post-trained derivative of FlashX. Exact legal-model parameter count, public weights, and weight license not independently verified; an official-publisher exact checkpoint query returned no matches. General Flash family's architecture or open-source comparison language does not supply an exact legal weight license.[1][4]

